{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>May He judge between us.</b> The one who slackens against his fellow." "<b>The god of their father.</b> Serves for both sacred and profane. <b>And Jacob swore by the Fear of his father Isaac.</b> He did not wish to mention HaShem after the profane that Laban mentioned." "<b>By the Fear of his father Isaac.</b> This is a designation of divinity, that is, he swore by the god of his father Isaac, in his reverence — that is, בפחד אביו. And the Targum proves it: בדחיל לה יצחק. And a similar usage we find many in the language of Talmud and in the language of Scripture, יובילו שי למורא. Another interpretation: Jacob reminded Laban of the trembling that his father Isaac trembled at the time he came to curse him, for taking the blessings by cunning, as it is written: ויחרד יצחק — to say, even his father, who is a complete righteous man, sensed something within himself when he came to do him harm." "<b>[And swore.</b> And fulfilled.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:00.962432298Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}